  "narrative": "Fresh-reset precondition passed: resolve_replay_plan({\"game\":\"bp35\",\"levels_reproduced\":5}, Path(\".\")) returned the 164-action banked plan, and replay reached frame_level(frame)==5. The established L6 route was then reproduced exactly: click the two lower X blocks at display (39,51) and (45,51), move right three columns, click the first cyan switch at (39,33), move right into the shaft, move left until blocked, and click the second switch at its camera-adjusted position (27,29). This reached the protected notch at player world position (5,30), camera 144, with upward gravity active. Compact frame diffs and object tuples were used from there. ACTION1/ACTION2/wait, clicking the consumed switch, clicking the goal, clicking the left partition, and attempting an off-screen click of the orange-outlined object all produced no puzzle-state change. Reopening and reclosing the right lower X shield proved that its open state is a pillar hazard. ACTION7 unexpectedly behaved as bounded undo and reversed those toggle changes, correcting the prior no-op classification. No safe exit was executed before the cumulative 700 env.step call ceiling was reached, so max_level_reached remains 5 and reproduction_verified is false for a new win. The most promising next-round hypothesis is to click the second gravity switch one or two columns earlier (while the player is still under the x=6/x=7 shields), avoiding the need for the known-lethal lateral step from x=5 after reversal.",
